# Shell scripts run under WSL dash, which fatals on CRLF ("set: Illegal
# option -"). Pin them to LF so no Windows-side editor or checkout can
# reintroduce it (it did once, at the M1 fix wave -- msys sh masked it).
*.sh text eol=lf
# cmd.exe batch files are the mirror case: label/goto parsing wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Parity prompt files are consumed as raw bytes (the file IS the prompt;
# MANIFEST token counts are computed over exactly these bytes). Exempt them
# from ALL eol conversion so no checkout can rewrite \n into \r\n and
# silently change tokenization under the parity gate.
tests/data/parity/*.txt -text
# Same rule for the W1 validation prompts: their committed oracle JSON
# captures and ref outputs correspond to these exact bytes.
tests/tooling/validation/*.txt -text
# The HTTP garbage corpus IS its bytes. Several fixtures exist precisely to
# carry a bare LF, a bare CR, or a CRLF split across a read boundary, and eol
# conversion would rewrite the defect out of them on checkout -- turning a
# fixture into a different test while its name still claims the old one. The
# damage would appear only on a fresh clone, never in the tree that wrote them.
tests/data/http_corpus/*.raw -text

# Every *.golden is compared BYTE FOR BYTE against what a gate generates at run
# time, and every generator here writes LF (main.c puts stdout in binary mode on
# Windows precisely so it does). Left unpinned, core.autocrlf=true rewrites them
# to CRLF ON CHECKOUT and the diff then reports every line as changed -- so a
# fresh Windows clone fails all five golden gates while the tree that wrote them
# stays green. Measured with `git checkout-index` on 2026-08-29: unpinned, this
# checkout turns tests/data/serve.golden into 86 CRLF lines.
tests/data/*.golden -text
# ⚠ THE PATTERN ABOVE DOES NOT REACH A SUBDIRECTORY, and the generation-parity
# goldens live in one. Without these two lines a fresh Windows clone
# (core.autocrlf=true here) rewrites them to CRLF on checkout and
# tests/llama_gen_golden.sh fails every case, while the tree that wrote them
# stays green -- the precise failure the paragraph above was written about,
# reappearing one directory deeper.
tests/data/llama_gen/*.golden -text
# And the prompts are exempt for the same reason tests/data/parity/*.txt is:
# the file IS the prompt, so rewriting \n to \r\n changes the tokenization and
# therefore what the model is asked, silently, on checkout only.
tests/data/llama_gen/*.txt -text
